3. Apache-2.0 dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Seamline links against Apache-2.0-licensed dependencies at build and runtime.
As of the last run of `node scripts/license-gate.mjs --notices`, none of the
Apache-2.0 packages in the installed tree ships a NOTICE file of its own, so
there are no upstream attribution notices to reproduce verbatim here. The
dependencies themselves are recorded, in full and with versions, in
`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt`.

Two Apache-2.0 build dependencies are called out explicitly because a previous
revision of this project's design recorded their licence incorrectly
(v3 section 10.2):

  - LinkML (https://github.com/linkml/linkml) is Apache-2.0, not CC0. Only
    `linkml-model` and `linkml-runtime` are CC0. Seamline uses LinkML as a
    build-time generator for the ontology; the generated artefacts are
    Seamline's own output, but the tooling's Apache-2.0 attribution obligation
    is recorded here rather than assumed away.

