4. No code derivation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Seamline implements published formats and aligns with published vocabularies.
It does not incorporate source code from any of them. Every prior-art
relationship is classified `SPEC-COMPATIBLE` or `CODE-DERIVED` in the design
record (v3 section 10.1), and as of this release every row is
`SPEC-COMPATIBLE`.

Specifically: no source has been copied from FINOS CALM, Backstage, Apache
Atlas, Cartography, OpenLineage, Joern, SCIP, Graphify, or any other
Apache-2.0 project. Implementing a published schema or reusing a vocabulary
term is not code derivation; copying an implementation is, and would carry the
upstream licence and its NOTICE with it. If that ever changes, the derived
files keep their upstream licence headers and this section must list them
before the change is merged.

